# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# One job: keep the apex on www, which is what the canonical link and og:url in
# index.html both declare and what Vercel answers today with a 308. Losing this
# would split the site across two hostnames and duplicate every crawled URL.
#
# On Vercel this was a dashboard domain setting rather than a line in
# vercel.json, which is exactly why it is easy to drop in a migration. It is
# written down here so it cannot be.
#
# Pages honours the same 308 (permanent, method-preserving) that Vercel used.
# The :splat carries the rest of the path through unchanged.
https://carta-europetravel.com/* https://www.carta-europetravel.com/:splat 308

# There is deliberately no SPA catch-all (`/* /index.html 200`) here.
#
# The app is one client-rendered URL: every route lives in the hash or the query
# string, and src only ever reads window.location.pathname and writes it back
# unchanged. Nothing needs a rewrite. Adding one would make every missing data
# shard answer 200 with the HTML shell instead of a clean 404, so a stale or
# mistyped shard path would parse as HTML rather than fail loudly. If real path
# routing ever lands (scripts/prerender.mjs, per the optimization report), add
# the fallback then and scope it to the prerendered paths, never to /*.
